## The beats

### 0 · The report that starts it — lending analytics
Open the deployment's playground link and go to **`/analytics`** — the weekly risk
report Lending Analytics sends **AI Engineering**: appeals climbing, decision CSAT breaking down,
approval rate on eligible BEVs collapsing, **€-volume walking away** — while the agent's own quality
monitors are **all green**. Every figure is derived from the same deterministic plan the seed
ingested. This is a cached historical snapshot; live submissions and disputes do not update it.
The appeal percentage is `user_disagreement = true` among **reviewed decisions**, not all applications.
> This is how it starts in real life: the business sees it first. Nothing the AI team watches is red.

### 1 · Dashboard — the only smoke
Open the dashboard{{ dashboard_link }}. Point out the **rising `user_disagreement` among reviewed decisions**
over the last {{ drift_window_days }} days — while **`answer_quality`, `tone`, `format_compliance` stay green**.
> Quality looks fine. The only signal something's wrong is that people keep appealing.

